Intercom local/cloud speech and wake-word qualification

Workstream ID: ic-05
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/4
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Evidence-backed speech selection and wake conversation contract
Dependencies: ic-01

Purpose:
  Compare local and cloud speech before selection and qualify local wake-only
  standby. The owner's later request selects installed local English speech
  and click-on/click-off capture for a bounded prototype; no cloud audio or wake
  standby is authorized by that exception.

Tasks:
  [x] Reopen the selected mic once after a structured Intercom clarification,
      only after local question playback completes (or written display when
      muted). Keep the question and bounded follow-up context, cancellation,
      playback-stop/opt-out/stale guards, readiness checks and transcript review.
      Ordinary replies and permission prompts must not start capture.
  [x] Package reusable native recognition and verify the same resident model
      across local check, live drafts and final audio, with awaited shutdown.
  [x] Support up to five minutes of local push-to-talk audio across capture,
      validated PCM transport and both recognition engines. Auto-cutoff must
      preserve a reviewable transcript without dispatch; retain cancellation,
      request-size guards and the running portable. Qualify boundary/overrun
      cases, long recorded input and disposable desktop finalization.
  [x] Qualify owner-recorded English input through local check/live/final paths,
      cancellation, low-rate review and recovery without cloud audio.
  [x] Bundle pinned local recognition for the owner's next candidate and verify
      a fresh profile works without choosing folders or seeding engine settings.
  [x] Record approval for local multilingual downloads and Roman Hinglish output.
  [x] Add and synthetically exercise pinned artifact checks and disk-free CLI JSON transport.
  [x] Build the pinned source unchanged and verify actual AMD Vulkan inference.
  [x] Connect explicit pinned local model setup and recognition; retain Windows only by choice.
  [x] Add measured microphone format/signal checks and a strictly local speech
      test that preserves the working draft and cannot dispatch requests.
  [x] Persist explicit English/Hindi/auto language selection and force review
      for below-16kHz audio; this mitigates, not fixes, the failed8kHz name gate.
  [ ] Provide a qualified install/distribution path beyond prepared-folder selection.
  [ ] Qualify disfluencies, negations, corrections and technical/session names.
  [ ] Preserve raw meaning through Roman-script normalization without cloud audio.
  [x] Implement the selected installed-Windows English push-to-talk prototype.
  [x] Verify local recognition retains multiple phrases through stream completion.
  [ ] Select test hardware, languages, phrase, datasets and resource/latency budgets.
  [ ] Obtain audio/provider consent and choose one viable local/cloud candidate.
  [ ] Verify exact model/voice licenses, packaging and provider data/cost terms.
  [ ] Measure wake/recognition errors, response timing and concurrent resources.
  [ ] Qualify speed-first defaults and compare selectable processing priorities.
  [ ] Test echo, speech interruption, device loss and offline behavior.
  [ ] Qualify Windows endpoint AEC and label any half-duplex fallback honestly.
  [ ] Record human listening results and an explicit provider/privacy decision.

Acceptance criteria:
  Clarification replies use bounded capture, not continuous listening. Stop,
  cancellation, hidden windows and failed playback cannot arm a pending mic;
  no listening before readiness or automatic permission approval.
  Bounded long-capture slice: up to300s is accepted across renderer/host/native;
  one extra sample is rejected at the host. Cutoff preserves a reviewable
  transcript without automatic dispatch; cancellation and destination-size
  guards remain. Full-input completion is not recognition-quality acceptance.
  Same-scenario comparison distinguishes facts, measurements and user preference.
  Wake standby stays local; the chosen phrase and timeout are documented.
  No silent cloud failover or raw-audio persistence by default.
  Voice activity detection is not represented as echo cancellation/authentication.
  Local speech is not misrepresented as fully offline Copilot execution.
  Results and selected contracts inform ic-02 before desktop implementation.
  Performance/speed is evaluated first; error rates and useful-response latency
  are reported together, not just time to a generic acknowledgment.
  Native binding support is not exact model/license/device qualification.

